## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical exposure to real-world channel effects (convolutional mixing) and online adaptation. It probes choices about frequency-domain vs time-domain solutions, how to maintain permutation consistency across bins, and pragmatic latency/evaluation constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Convolutive blind source separation
- Online whitening and adaptive updating
- Per-bin ICA vs joint diagonalization across frequencies
- Cross-bin permutation alignment and latency constraints

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code sketch
while (streaming) {
  let X = STFT(frame);
  W = updateWhitening(X);
  Y = ICA(X, W); // per-frequency or joint-diagonalized
  alignPermutations(Y);
  x_hat = iSTFT(Y);
}
``` 

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate permutation stability over time?
- What happens if the reverberation time changes quickly, and how would you adapt?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a practical online ICA pipeline under real-time constraints and nonstationary audio. It also probes decisions about whitening, joint diagonalization, and permutation under resource limits, plus simple robustness and evaluation plan.

## Key Concepts
- Online whitening with forgetting factor
- Joint diagonalization vs per-bin ICA
- Cross-bin permutation using magnitude/phase cues
- Outlier handling for impulsive wind noise
- Embedded latency constraints
- Ground-truth based evaluation

## Code Example
```javascript
for (let t of frames) {
  const X = STFT(t)
  const W = updateWhitening(X, α)
  const Y = Demix(W, X)
  const P = alignPermutation(Y)
  const Z = IFFT(P * Y)
  output(Z)
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale to 4+ microphones and more sources?
- How would you quantify robustness to varying wind conditions across environments?

## Why This Is Asked

Car environments introduce dynamic geometry, intermittent sensor faults, and real-time constraints. This question probes the ability to design an online ICA solution that adapts to changing mixing, handles missing data gracefully, and maintains consistent source order over time.

## Key Concepts

- Online sliding-window ICA with adaptive whitening
- Kalman-style demixer updates on whitened data
- Missing-channel handling via subspace completion without reinitialization
- Permutation stability using short temporal memory and cross-frame non-Gaussianity cues
- Real-time latency targets and robust evaluation (ground-truth SDR/SIR, perceptual checks)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: online update for W on whitened data Xw
function onlineUpdate(W, Xw, lr) {
  const Y = W.dot(Xw);
  const e = gradientNonGaussianity(Y);
  return W.add(e.mul(lr).dot(Xw.transpose()));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you diagnose instability when sources cross or when dropouts occur?
- How would you scale to larger arrays with nonuniform sampling or asynchronous microphones?
